  "conversation": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "user": "I need the wall ready for finishing quickly. How does block installation compare with cast-in-situ curing?",
      "assistant": "For speed, pre-cast hemp-lime blocks are generally favored because they arrive already cured. Once they are laid with lime mortar, you only need to wait about 2 to 3 days for the mortar to set before you can move on to plastering and finishing. \n\nIn contrast, cast-in-situ (monolithic) hemp-lime is tamped wet into formwork. While the forms can often come off the next day, the material itself requires a natural curing window of about 3 to 6 weeks for drying and carbonation before you can safely apply final finishes. Since your priority is speed, pre-cast blocks will get your walls ready for finishing much faster.\n\nWould you like to calculate the wall volume for a specific project size to compare material quantities?"
    }
